{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:4c0e132089e34987","name":"Falling Damage","source":{"id":"source:reference-4c0e132089e34987","title":"Falling Damage","revision":18166,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T19:41:56Z","sha256":"209955366b1ac2d0bc185779b1f2393512a62930707214da0219d326b8a92704","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18166","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Falling%20Damage&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-4c0e132089e34987","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When a creature, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"},", or object falls, make an attack roll (1d20+20) against its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},". If the attack succeeds, the target takes 1d6 points of damage for every 3 meters fallen (to a maximum of 20d6 damage). If the attack fails, the target only takes half damage. A falling creature or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," also lands ",{"tag":"a","children":["Prone"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Prone","referenceId":"reference:4d99dff1fb964110"},". (A falling ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," falls 150 meters (100 squares) when it is ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disabled"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disabled"},", plus another 300 meters (200 squares) every round until it hits the surface.)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["If a character is ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trained"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained"}," in the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Acrobatics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Acrobatics","referenceId":"reference:0d0b7eee2953750e"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jump"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jump","referenceId":"reference:9ee0ca3e24d60ea0"}," Skills, it can reduce the damage it takes from a fall with a successful skill check (see ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reduce Falling Damage"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reduce_Falling_Damage"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jump Down"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jump_Down"}," for more details). If the check succeeds and it takes no damage from the fall, it lands on its feet. If a character falls from a height of greater than 60 meters, treat the fall as being only 60 meters for the purposes of reducing Falling Distance.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Falling Objects"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Just as creatures take damage when they fall, so too do they take damage when hit by Falling Objects. When a creature could be hit by a Falling Object, make an attack roll (using the attack bonus listed in the table below) against the target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},". If the attack succeeds, the target takes the listed damage. If the attack fails, the target takes half damage instead. This is considered an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Area Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Area_Attack"},". Objects of Fine and Diminutive size are too small to deal damage, regardless of the distance fallen. A Falling Object must land wholly or partly in a target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fighting Space"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fighting_Space","referenceId":"reference:cdbf34043baceb78"}," to deal damage to the target.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The GM may adjust the damage depending on the circumstances. For example, a Colossal object might be extremely light (such as a gas-filled passenger balloon). Objects that are forced downward (such as a piston in a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," factory or a closing door) deal damage as if they were two size categories larger than they actually are. Additionally, if the target is at least three size categories smaller than the Falling Object, the target cannot move unless it succeeds on a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," check to lift the object off itself (see the table below for the check DC) or a DC 15 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Acrobatics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Acrobatics","referenceId":"reference:0d0b7eee2953750e"}," check to crawl out from underneath. The GM can modify the DCs for either check based on the circumstances; for example, a character might find themselves trapped under an object that has opening or gaps that allow them to wiggle free.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["OBJECT SIZE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["EXAMPLE(S)\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["ATTACK BONUS\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["DAMAGE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["STRENGTH"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/STRENGTH"}," CHECK DC\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Tiny\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Pistol"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Pistol","referenceId":"reference:38dcc06542ba096c"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Datapad"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Datapad","referenceId":"reference:7a32da74ac188805"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1d4\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Small\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Rifle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Rifle","referenceId":"reference:fb78a988cbf9557f"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-2\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1d6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Medium\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Locker, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Armor","referenceId":"reference:4bc2d20a5687b54f"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+0\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2d6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["5\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Large\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Speeder Bike"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speeder_Bike"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+2\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["4d6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["10\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Huge\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Landspeeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Landspeeder"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["8d6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["15\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Gargantuan\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+10\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["12d6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["20\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Colossal\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["AT-AT"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/AT-AT","referenceId":"reference:72b76e7d76526ae5"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+20\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["20d6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["25\n"]}]}]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
